  "narration_beats": [
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_001",
      "attaches_to": "state",
      "target_id": "state_000",
      "text": "By the end of this video, you'll have the Customers table open in DB Browser for SQLite, looking at its raw rows and columns.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 24,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_002",
      "attaches_to": "state",
      "target_id": "state_000",
      "text": "Opening a table shows you the data exactly as it's stored, before any sorting or filtering changes what you see. That matters here because if you trust a sorted or filtered view by mistake, you could think the Customers table has fewer records than it really does.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 47,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_003",
      "attaches_to": "edge",
      "target_id": "edge_001",
      "text": "Click the Browse Data tab near the top of the window.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 11,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_004",
      "attaches_to": "edge",
      "target_id": "edge_002",
      "text": "Click the table dropdown menu.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 5,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_005",
      "attaches_to": "edge",
      "target_id": "edge_003",
      "text": "Select the Customers table from the list.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 7,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_006",
      "attaches_to": "edge",
      "target_id": "edge_004",
      "text": "Wait for the table to load.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 6,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_007",
      "attaches_to": "state",
      "target_id": "state_004",
      "text": "What you're looking at is a data grid, a spreadsheet-style object where each row is one customer record and each column is one attribute, like name or email. The status bar at the bottom of the window confirms 500 rows and 6 columns for this Customers table.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 47,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_008",
      "attaches_to": "state",
      "target_id": "state_004",
      "text": "You've now confirmed the Customers table holds 500 rows across 6 columns, untouched and unsorted. Next, you'll sort the Orders table by order_date in ascending order using the column header.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 30,
      "start_time": 0.0,
